# Build context exclusions.
#
# .gitignore has NO effect on a Docker build context: `COPY dashboard
# ./dashboard` happily copies `dashboard/.env`, and app.py loads it at import,
# so a local build bakes live credentials into the image and the process reads
# them as if an operator had set them. (Render builds from the Git clone, where
# .env was never committed, so prod images are unaffected -- but a local image
# must never be pushed to a registry, and the no-credential path cannot be
# tested while the key ships inside.)
#
# Secrets first.
#
# ⚠ Docker ignore patterns are NOT .gitignore patterns: one without a slash
# matches only at the context ROOT, so a bare `.env` leaves `dashboard/.env`
# -- the one app.py actually loads -- in the image. The `**/` forms are the
# ones that do the work here; the bare forms are kept for the root copies.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
credentials/
**/credentials/
*.pem
*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Version control and tooling metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.pytest_cache

# Virtual environments -- the image builds its own isolated ones.
.venv
venv
.ai-hedge-fund-venv
.tradingagents-venv

# Caches and build junk.
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Local databases and scratch data.
#
# ⚠ `*.db` is deliberately NOT here. `dashboard/storage/data/backtest.db` is
# committed and holds the seed runs `dashboard/config/defaults.json`
# references; on Render, which has no persistent disk, that file is what
# DATABASE_PATH resets to on every deploy. Excluding the extension would ship
# an image whose seed data is missing, and a developer's working copy cannot
# be told from the seed by extension. `test_docker_build_context.py` asserts
# the seed file stays in the context, because adding `*.db` here looks like a
# tidy-up and is a regression.
#
# The recursive forms below are load-bearing, for the reason the header gives:
# a slashless pattern anchors at the context ROOT, so `*.db-journal` alone
# left `dashboard/storage/data/backtest.db-journal` in the image.
*.db-journal
**/*.db-journal
*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite
*.log
**/*.log
